cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "TBMD: Tensor-Based Modal Decomposition Method"
type: software
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/denis-samatov/tensor-based-modal-decomposition-method"
abstract: >-
  Python library for tensor-based modal decomposition, sparse sensor placement and field
  reconstruction. Release 2.1.0 adds the Brugge sparse-sensing study package
  (studies/brugge_sparse_sensing) that generates every number, table and figure of the manuscript
  "Sparse-sensor reconstruction of reservoir states with tensor-based and matrix modal bases: a
  reproducible benchmark on the Brugge model". The Brugge simulation inputs are not included.
keywords:
  - reservoir monitoring
  - sensor placement
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - Tucker decomposition
  - compressive sensing
